WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.434
Nikki Haley and Ron DeSantis, Trump's

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.669
top rivals for the GOP

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.770
presidential nomination.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.305
They're heating up their attacks on him

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.573
on the campaign trail.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.407
They're not attacking him.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.376
On January six, new polling

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:11.211
shows less and less GOP voters

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.045
who are fewer

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.880
think Trump was responsible for the riot.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.248
And a new Washington Post

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.717
poll finds only 14% of Republicans

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.319
believe he has a great deal

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.121
or good amount of responsibility.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:23.189
And that's a drop from 27%

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.791
just two years ago.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:25.558
Today, Nikki

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:26.960
Haley will be in the early

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.428
voting state of New Hampshire,

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.764
while DeSantis focuses on Iowa.

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:32.132
And their big push comes

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:34.734
just 12 days before the Iowa caucuses.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.737
As Trump continues to dominate the polls,

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.806
we have a countdown clock.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:40.673
Steve can turn on notes

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:41.708
about the countdown clocks

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.742
he can turn to joins us

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.144
live, starting us off this hour

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.145
from Iowa.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:48.348
We all are aware that it is almost time.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:49.783
Nikki Haley, Ron DeSantis out

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:50.683
with ads targeting

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:51.985
one another, taking some swings

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.153
at Trump last night

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.854
in their town halls and their events.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.389
Are we seeing movement on the

00:00:56.389 --> 00:01:00.827
ground before these caucuses?

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:01.728
Well, we'll

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:02.962
find out in 12 days, Phil,

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:03.596
whether or not

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.532
these caucus goers here in Iowa

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.033
are moved at all by these

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.468
these overtures from DeSantis

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.335
and Nikki Haley.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.603
They have struck this balance

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.438
where they have decided

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:13.373
that they cannot overtly attack

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.507
Trump on one of his biggest

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.809
vulnerabilities, this

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.710
the January six riots.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.179
These ballot problems

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.780
he's having getting on the ballots.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.182
Instead, they've actually defended him.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:22.715
And in fact,

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.483
in the last couple of weeks

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.584
to Santos and Haley have said

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.119
they would even pardon Trump

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:26.886
if it got to that point.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:27.754
But here's one area

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.155
they have challenged

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.824
Trump on, is that his decision

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.826
to not show up to any of these debates.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:33.693
DeSantis and Haley,

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:34.294
of course,

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:37.130
will appear at our CNN debate next week

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.798
just ahead of these Iowa caucuses.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.300
Trump will not be there again.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.334
Instead will be holding

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.203
counterprogramming on Fox News.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.737
Here's what the is said on Fox

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.873
News himself about this, about Trump

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:50.710
deciding to duck, to debate once again.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.845
Why shouldn't he have

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:52.912
to answer questions?

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.180
I mean, he's running on things

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.915
like deporting illegals

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:56.850
and building a wall.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.418
But he did that in 16

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.452
and didn't get it done.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.286
So I think he owes

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.222
answers to those questions.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.957
He has not been willing to do that.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.425
Obviously, if you go by polling,

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.025
it hasn't hurt.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:06.693
But I think

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.794
now that we're in the new year,

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:08.761
I think voters

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.797
do expect you to answer those questions.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.165
I think Iowans expect you

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:16.636
to show up and debate.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.371
The scientists will be right behind me

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.106
at this community center in Waukee,

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:21.241
Iowa, later today,

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.542
where he will be trying to convince

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.344
Iowans that it's time to move on

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:25.345
from Donald Trump,

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.579
that this inability to

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.481
or unwillingness to debate

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.616
is a character flaw.

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.184
And it shows that he is not ready

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:31.885
for the challenge of

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.753
going up against President Biden

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.054
and carrying the mantle

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.823
for the Republican in another election.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:37.557
Phil?

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:38.691
All right, Steve Cantorial for us

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.627
live in Waukee, Iowa. Thank you.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:41.828
And Ron DeSantis and Nikki

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:42.662
Haley take questions

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.897
directly from Iowa voters

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.131
in back to back events.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:45.899
The CNN Republican

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:47.400
presidential town halls moderated

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.568
by our own Kaitlan Collins

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:49.068
and Erin BURNETT.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.603
They are live tomorrow night

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.172
starting at nine Eastern.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.207
New developments this morning in former

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.275
President Trump's battle

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.443
to stay on the ballot in Maine.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.511
Trump formally appealed

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.012
to the state

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.346
superior Court Tuesday

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.614
to reverse the decision

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.483
by Democratic Secretary of State

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:04.350
Gina Bellows,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.019
who determined Trump

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:07.220
is an insurrectionist

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.522
and is constitutionally barred

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.657
from appearing on the state's

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:11.858
primary ballot.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.159
Trump's team argues

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.494
that Bellows is a, quote,

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.862
biased decision maker

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.864
and has no jurisdiction in the matter.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:20.500
CNN's Zachary Cohen joins us now.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.435
Can you tell us a little more detail

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.237
about the president's

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:27.073
legal appeal when it comes to Maine?

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:27.840
Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.641
The Trump

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.076
team is attacking

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:32.512
the secretary of state, as you mentioned,

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:34.013
accusing her of being biased

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:34.347
and saying

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:35.481
that she doesn't have the authority

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.816
to make this decision

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:37.884
to remove him from the ballot.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:38.851
Now, we have to remember that

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:39.986
Maine is unique in that

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.287
the process dictates

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.555
that the secretary of state

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:43.656
is the first stop

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:44.224
or questions

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.558
about whether or not someone

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.826
can be taken off the ballot.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.094
And from there,

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:49.996
if appealed, it goes to the court,

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.631
which is what we're seeing happen now.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.566
But in Maine, also to the argument

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.602
that Trump is submitting here is he's

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:56.869
attacking something at the core

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.171
of what the secretary of state's decision

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:58.938
was, that he says

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.273
I'm not an insurrectionist.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.842
He really refutes that point outright.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.444
And that is really at the center

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.779
of this section of the 14th Amendment

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.881
that has really not just been,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.515
you know,

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:10.750
the reason that the decision

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.517
was reached in Maine,

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.353
but also in some other states as well.

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.821
So now the Maine Superior Court

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.589
has about 20 days

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.424
until it can issue its decision.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:18.858
From there,

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:21.060
it would go to the Maine Supreme Court,

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:21.461
which has

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:23.029
until the last day of this month

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.731
to make its decision.

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:26.532
Zach, on Colorado,

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.667
Do we have any sense in terms

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.502
of what the effect of an appeal

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:30.570
will actually have, what it will

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.206
set off in terms of process?

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:33.906
Absolutely.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.041
If and when Trump

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.110
does appeal the Colorado decision,

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.911
which is similar to the Maine decision

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.114
and why it removed Trump from the ballot,

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:41.981
it would essentially jump

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:44.784
the Maine decision in what it would be

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.352
because it would go directly to the US

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:46.986
Supreme Court.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:47.720
And look,

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.989
any decision by the US Supreme Court

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:51.891
would be the final say on this issue.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:52.859
But that remains to be seen

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.527
if the US Supreme Court

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.195
will ultimately take up this case.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.530
There's been mounting pressure

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.031
for them to do

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:59.065
so as states have been

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.366
litigating this on their own

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:01.301
and honestly coming up

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.869
with a variety of different views

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:03.569
and opinions on it.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:04.304
So, you know,

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:05.471
there are some state officials

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:06.572
that are even calling

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.707
for the US Supreme Court

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:08.641
to add some clarity,

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.309
bring some clarity

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.577
to this situation with the election

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.179
looming. So closely.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:13.946
One more thing.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.915
Can you articulate this immunity

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.750
claim from the Trump team

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.818
and kind of how

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:21.487
they're doubling down on it?

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:22.055
So in the

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:23.856
federal case, the federal criminal case,

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.158
this is the one overseen

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.694
by special counsel Jack Smith and relates

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:28.728
to Donald Trump's

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:29.762
election subversion,

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.998
alleged crimes in that case.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:33.299
Donald Trump is defending himself

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:33.900
by saying, look,

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:34.734
I should absolutely

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.736
I should enjoy absolute immunity

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:37.570
and presidents

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.705
should be protected

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:39.572
from any act,

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:41.007
from any criminal prosecution

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:42.442
on acts that they committed

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:43.142
or that they took

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:43.743
that took place

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.078
while they were president.

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:45.778
Now, this is a really

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:46.813
controversial argument,

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:48.348
a sweeping immunity

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:49.816
claim that Jack Smith himself

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:51.117
has forcefully pushed back

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:53.086
on Trump, reiterating that last night

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:54.387
that everything that he did

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:56.022
in the aftermath of the 2020 election

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.057
he was doing in his official capacity

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:58.725
as president

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.093
and therefore should not be able

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.627
to be prosecuted for it.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:04.364
Zachary Cohen, thanks for explaining

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:05.331
what former President Trump

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:06.632
aims to win back the White House.

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.934
Despite facing those 91

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:08.768
criminal indictments

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:10.136
and countless controversies.

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:11.304
The Washington Post.

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:12.772
Really, really interesting

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:13.806
deep dive detailing, quote,

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:14.407
how Trump

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:15.775
reignited his base

00:06:15.775 --> 00:06:16.642
and took control

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:17.643
of the Republican primary.

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:18.611
Now, the piece notes

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:19.946
Trump has turned his criminal indictments

00:06:19.946 --> 00:06:20.913
into a rallying cry.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:22.615
His GOP opposition has so far

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:24.016
failed to coalesce around

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:26.252
a single effective message or challenger,

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:27.153
and his political operation

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.421
has been more professional

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:30.223
and disciplined than the past.

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:30.590
Joining us

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:31.791
now is Isaac Art Stauffer,

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:32.959
national political reporter

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:34.160
for The Washington Post,

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.595
one of the three bylines on a very,

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:36.662
very good piece this morning.

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:37.363
He's also

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:38.364
the author of Finish

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:39.632
What We Started the MAGA Movement's

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:41.467
Ground War to End Democracy.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.335
Also with us

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:44.070
is CNN political commentator and former

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:44.537
Trump White House

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:45.338
communications director.

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:46.239
Illicit affair Griffin.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.441
Guys, thanks so much for joining us.

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:50.309
As I was fascinated by this piece,

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:51.344
because I don't

00:06:51.344 --> 00:06:51.944
think people

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:52.745
remember that

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:55.114
when Trump announced that he was running,

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:57.483
it was not at a moment of

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:59.452
it wasn't a pinnacle moment

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:03.022
like the Mar a Lago room was half empty.

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:04.023
People didn't really think

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:04.690
he had a lot of juice

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.660
coming out of the midterms. What changed?

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.127
Right.

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.562
It was an unusually

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:11.431
weak moment for him politically.

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.732
The room wasn't half empty,

00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:14.300
but it was kind of padded

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.102
with the front row Joes

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:17.737
and the kind of other

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:18.938
MAGA super fans

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:20.039
and what you were missing

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:21.474
were like Republican elected

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:23.876
officials who were or major donors

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:24.977
who were staying away.

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:26.546
And then you have to remember,

00:07:26.546 --> 00:07:27.613
like the first thing he did

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.450
after launching was have dinner

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.251
with Kanye West and Nick Fuentes

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:33.219
and say he wanted

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:34.720
to terminate the Constitution.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.055
So things did not get off

00:07:36.055 --> 00:07:38.925
to a great start for the Trump campaign.

00:07:38.925 --> 00:07:41.594
And you probably wouldn't have predicted

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:43.296
that this is where they would be now.

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:44.997
So a bunch of things changed.

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.799
One is that

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:49.402
the Trump opposition within the party

